#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cono-check — Cono's checking component as a local web app.

The browser shows live video of your page (getUserMedia — any camera it
can see, including iPhone Continuity). Nothing streams anywhere: the page
diffs the video locally, and only when you pause writing does it snap one
full-resolution frame and send it here, where Claude (`claude` CLI — your
Claude Code login, no API key) reads it and reports:

  visibility n/10   what the camera can actually see
  on your page      faithful transcription, student's errors preserved
  check             hint-first: where the mistake is, never the answer

Usage:
  cono-check                     # the Desk View camera (top-down on your desk) - the default
  cono-check browser             # fallback: any browser camera (iPhone Continuity, webcam)
  cono-check session             # 10-minute recorded session (Desk View)
  cono-check demo                # no camera needed: bundled sample session (demo chem = chemistry)
  cono-check doctor              # preflight: is everything ready to run?
  cono-check --model opus        # pick the model (default: sonnet)
  cono-check --model ollama:qwen3.5:9b   # local open model via Ollama (app running, `ollama pull qwen3.5:9b`)
  cono-check --replay DIR        # replay any recorded session directory
  cono-check --port 9000
  cono-check --no-open           # don't open the browser automatically
Ctrl-C to stop.
"""
